   "i": 82,
   "shape_h": "p",
   "shape_m": "p",
   "html_text": "The content of a sentence, at a context, can also be evaluated for truth at a world other than the world of the context. This is how the truth-values of sentences that contain modal operators, such as ‘possible’, are determined. For example, the content of ‘I am a philosopher’, with respect to ⟦M⟧ , is the singular proposition that Mary is a philosopher. This proposition is true at ⟦M⟧ , the world of context ⟦M⟧ . But this proposition is false at world, ⟦M⟧ , in which Mary goes into mathematics ",
